🚽 #375: a write to a member of a deadass struct must be rejected during
🚽 semantic analysis, so the program never starts running and the yapping()
🚽 below never executes. Covers a direct member write and a nested member
🚽 chain, whose root is found by recursing through the inner member access.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};
gang Outer {
    gang Point inner;
};

skibidi main {
    deadass gang Point p;
    deadass gang Outer o;
    yapping("side effect");
    p.x = 2;
    o.inner.x = 3;
    bussin 0;
}
